{
  "tema": 5057,
  "slug": "apocope-buen-mal-gran",
  "titulo": "Bueno, malo, grande become buen, mal, gran before a noun",
  "subtitulo": "Un buen día, un mal momento, una gran ciudad.",
  "foto": "t03.jpg",
  "regla": "Before a masculine singular noun, bueno → buen and malo → mal. Grande → gran before any singular noun, and it means great. Plurals don't shorten.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": "2026-10-10",
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Most adjectives go after the noun, but **bueno** and **malo** can go before it. Then, before a **masculine singular** noun, they shorten: **buen**, **mal**. Before a noun, they sound a bit stronger."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "tabla",
          "encabezados": [
            "After the noun",
            "Before the noun"
          ],
          "filas": [
            [
              "un hombre bueno",
              "un buen hombre"
            ],
            [
              "un día malo",
              "un mal día"
            ],
            [
              "una película buena",
              "una buena película (no change)"
            ],
            [
              "una época mala",
              "una mala época (no change)"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "With feminine nouns, they keep their full form: **buena**, **mala**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**Grande** shortens to **gran** before **any** singular noun, masculine or feminine. And its meaning changes: after the noun it's _big_; before the noun, **gran** means _great, fantastic_."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "tabla",
          "encabezados": [
            "After the noun",
            "Before the noun"
          ],
          "filas": [
            [
              "una ciudad grande (_big_)",
              "una gran ciudad (_great_)"
            ],
            [
              "un corazón grande",
              "un gran corazón (_generous_)"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Plurals never shorten: **buenos amigos**, **malas noticias**, **grandes ideas**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "This shortening is called **apócope**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: only the singular loses its tail. **Buen**, **mal** for boys; **gran** for everyone."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "Mi papá es un ==buen== hombre.",
              "en": "My dad is a good man."
            },
            {
              "es": "Esta es una ==buena== película.",
              "en": "This is a good movie."
            },
            {
              "es": "Hoy tuve un ==mal== día.",
              "en": "I had a bad day today."
            },
            {
              "es": "Esa fue una ==mala== época.",
              "en": "That was a bad time."
            },
            {
              "es": "Tijuana es una ==gran== ciudad.",
              "en": "Tijuana is a great city."
            },
            {
              "es": "Tijuana es una ciudad ==grande==.",
              "en": "Tijuana is a big city."
            },
            {
              "es": "Beto tiene un ==gran== corazón.",
              "en": "Beto has a big heart."
            },
            {
              "es": "Son ==buenos== amigos.",
              "en": "They're good friends."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
